-- title:
--   Removing a Frobenius twist from a lifting statement at a place
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` whose residue field $\kappa_A =$ `IsLocalRing.ResidueField A` has characteristic $p$, let $n$ be a natural number, and write $\sigma =$ `iterateFrobenius` $\kappa_A\,p\,n$ for the ring endomorphism $x \mapsto x^{p^n}$ of $\kappa_A$. Let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $\kappa_A$ which is elliptic, let $\beta$ be an additive endomorphism of the group of affine points $W(\kappa_A)$, and let $\beta'$ be an additive endomorphism of the points of the twist $W^{(\sigma)} = W.\mathrm{map}\,\sigma$ satisfying $\beta' \circ F = F \circ \beta$, where $F =$ `ratPointHom` $\sigma$ is the coordinatewise map $(x,y) \mapsto (\sigma x, \sigma y)$, $0 \mapsto 0$. Assume that $(W^{(\sigma)}, \beta')$ admits a lift at $A$, in the following sense: there are a Weierstrass curve $E'$ over $A$ whose reduction $E' \bmod \mathfrak{m}_A$ has nonzero discriminant, a Weierstrass variable change $v'$ over $\kappa_A$ with $v' \cdot (E' \bmod \mathfrak{m}_A) = W^{(\sigma)}$, and an additive endomorphism $\alpha'$ of the points of $E' \otimes_A \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying in `rationalHomSet`, i.e. either identically zero or given, off a finite set of $x$-coordinates, by substituting the coordinates into fixed quotients of bivariate polynomials over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, such that for every point $P$ of $E' \otimes_A \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ one has $(v')_*(\overline{\alpha'(P)}) = \beta'((v')_*(\overline{P}))$; here the bar is `reduceHom`, reducing a point with coordinates in $A$ coordinatewise and sending a point with non-integral coordinates to $0$, and $(v')_*$ is the inverse of the point bijection `equivOfVariableChangeEq` attached to the equality $v' \cdot (E' \bmod \mathfrak{m}_A) = W^{(\sigma)}$. Then $(W, \beta)$ admits a lift at $A$ in exactly the same sense: there exist $E$ over $A$ with $E \bmod \mathfrak{m}_A$ of nonzero discriminant, a variable change $v$ with $v \cdot (E \bmod \mathfrak{m}_A) = W$, and $\alpha \in$ `rationalHomSet` for $E \otimes_A \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $v_*(\overline{\alpha(P)}) = \beta(v_*(\overline{P}))$ for all points $P$.
--
--   This is the untwisting step in the Deuring-style lifting of an elliptic curve together with an endomorphism from the residue field of a place of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ to characteristic zero: liftability of a Frobenius twist $(W^{(\sigma)}, \beta')$ implies liftability of $(W, \beta)$, the transport being effected by an automorphism of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ preserving $A$ and inducing the desired automorphism of the (algebraically closed) residue field, as provided by [`ValuationSubring.exists_algEquiv_smul_eq_and_residue_eq_of_ringEquiv_residueField`](thm.html#ValuationSubring.exists_algEquiv_smul_eq_and_residue_eq_of_ringEquiv_residueField) and [`ValuationSubring.isAlgClosed_residueField_algebraicClosure_rat`](thm.html#ValuationSubring.isAlgClosed_residueField_algebraicClosure_rat). It is used in the characteristic-two lifting statement [`WeierstrassCurve.exists_variableChange_smul_eq_and_reduceHom_comp_eq_of_exists_reduceHom_comp_eq_two_smul_of_charP_two`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.exists_variableChange_smul_eq_and_reduceHom_comp_eq_of_exists_reduceHom_comp_eq_two_smul_of_charP_two).
